    "ancientarmory:ancientarmory-help-title": "Ancient Armory: Introduction",
    "ancientarmory:ancientarmory-help-text": "<strong>Ancient Armory</strong><br><br>This mod tweaks all the unused vanilla weapon models, and integrates them into the latest version for the game.<br>All items should be fully craftable, some with semi custom animations, like the <a href=\"handbooksearch://claymore\">claymore</a>.<br>Many of the original models are rescaled, balanced, and tweaked to better fit the games style, and gameplay.<br><br><strong>Weapon types</strong><br>There are currently several weapon types in this mod and thus, categorization is relevant if a player is using the Xskills or Level UP mod.<br><br>These weapons can be divided into the following categories:<br><br><strong>Axes</strong><br><a href=\"handbooksearch://bearded axe \">Bearded axe</a><br><a href=\"handbooksearch://battle axe \">Battle axe</a><br><a href=\"handbooksearch://bardiche \">Bardiche</a><br><br><strong>Swords</strong><br><a href=\"handbooksearch://Gladius \">Gladius</a><br><a href=\"handbooksearch://arming sword \">Arming Sword</a><br><a href=\"handbooksearch://Claymore \">Claymore</a><br><a href=\"handbooksearch://Sabre \">Sabre</a><br><a href=\"handbooksearch://longsword\">Longsword</a><br><a href=\"handbooksearch://falchion\">Falchion</a><br><a href=\"handbooksearch://flanged mace \">Flanged Mace</a>*<br><a href=\"handbooksearch://morningstar \">Morningstar</a>*<br><a href=\"handbooksearch://spiked mace \">Spiked Mace</a>*<br><a href=\"handbooksearch://warhammer \">Warhammer</a>*<br><br><strong>Knives</strong><br><a href=\"handbooksearch://dagger \">Dagger</a><br><a href=\"handbooksearch://stiletto \">Stiletto</a><br><a href=\"handbooksearch://khanjar \">Khanjar</a><br><a href=\"handbooksearch://baselard \">Baselard</a><br><br><strong>Spears</strong><br><a href=\"handbooksearch://boar \">Boar</a><br><a href=\"handbooksearch://voulge \">Voulge</a><br><a href=\"handbooksearch://fork \">Fork</a><br><a href=\"handbooksearch://ranseur \">Ranseur</a><br><br><strong>*</strong>Maces with the base game are counted as swords, with Combat Overhaul they are properly Maces."
}
